{
  "id": "phase-rs_phase_5406",
  "repo_name": "phase-rs/phase",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/phase-rs/phase",
  "base_commit": "2c61c66e65f20f40eafdf613ef28dd8216a78da6",
  "pr_number": 5406,
  "issue_number": 5392,
  "issue_title": "parser: compound-subject chosen-type static strict-fails (Rukarumel, Biologist)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`Rukarumel, Biologist`'s chosen-creature-type static \u2014 `Slivers you control and nontoken creatures you control are the chosen type in addition to their other creature types.` \u2014 is a **compound-subject** sibling of the \"chosen type\" static class (Arcane Adaptation, Xenograft, Lifecraft Engine), and it currently strict-fails: no `StaticDefinition` is produced at all (verified against `data/card-data.json`: `static_abilities: []`, the whole line collapses into an `Unimplemented` ability).\n\nThis is the same *structural* gap shape as #5219 (Life and Limb's compound-subject animation static): two subject clauses joined by \"and\", each individually already resolvable via an existing building block, but the combination unhandled by any dispatcher.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`parse_arcane_adaptation_chosen_type_static` (`crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_static/type_change.rs:94`) delegates subject-matching to `parse_chosen_creature_type_static_subject` (`type_change.rs:228-246`), which only recognizes three **fixed literal** single-subject forms:\n- `\"creatures you control are\"`\n- `\"each creature you control is\"`\n- `\"vehicle creatures you control are\"`\n\nRukarumel's subject \u2014 `\"Slivers you control and nontoken creatures you control\"` \u2014 matches none of these, so the predicate parser is never reached.\n\nBoth conjuncts are independently well-supported elsewhere:\n- `\"Slivers you control\"` \u2192 resolves via `parse_creature_subject_filter`/`parse_continuous_subject_filter` (subtype filter).\n- `\"nontoken creatures you control\"` \u2192 already has a direct regression test at `oracle_static/tests.rs:12291-12296` (`parse_continuous_subject_filter(\"Nontoken creatures you control\")`) confirming it resolves via `FilterProp::NonToken`.\n- The general \"`<X> you control and <Y> you control`\" compounding is already handled generically by `parse_controlled_compound_continuous_subject_filter` (`oracle_static/anthem.rs:616`), which `parse_continuous_subject_filter` already calls \u2014 but the chosen-type dispatcher never reaches that generic path because its subject matcher short-circuits on the fixed three-arm list first.\n\nThere's a second, smaller gap in the *predicate*: the addition-suffix matcher (`parse_chosen_creature_type_static_scope_body`, `type_change.rs:211-226`) only accepts `\"in addition to {their|its} other types\"`. Rukarumel's actual predicate is `\"in addition to their other **creature** types\"` (verified verbatim against Scryfall) \u2014 an extra `\"creature \"` word the current suffix grammar doesn't accept.\n\n## Verified card text (Scryfall, `oracleid: 84391c32-5bb7-4c36-be50-bbb5f8732156`)\n\n```\nAs Rukarumel enters, choose a creature type.\nSlivers you control and nontoken creatures you control are the chosen type in addition to their other creature types. The same is true for creature spells you control and creature cards you own that aren't on the battlefield.\n{3}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Sliver creature token.\n```\n\n- Sentence 1 (`As ~ enters, choose a creature type`) already parses correctly today (`replacements[0]`, `Choose { CreatureType, persist: true }` \u2014 CR 607.2d chosen-type link infra is unaffected).\n- Sentence 2's first clause (the compound-subject static, up to the first period) is the scope of this issue.\n- Sentence 2's trailing clause (`\"The same is true for creature spells you control and creature cards you own that aren't on the battlefield\"`) is a **pre-existing, separately-tracked gap**: applying continuous effects to non-battlefield zones isn't modeled yet, and this exact tail already appears \u2014 and is already left as a documented `Unimplemented` residual \u2014 on Arcane Adaptation and Maskwood Nexus (see the comment at `type_change.rs:253-256`). Out of scope here; should remain `Unimplemented` for Rukarumel too, consistent with its siblings.\n- The activated ability (`{3}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Sliver creature token.`) already parses correctly.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nAdd a compound-subject sibling dispatcher, mirroring #5219's shape:\n\n1. A shared `parse_chosen_type_addition_suffix` helper (CR 205.1a/b) \u2014 extracted from `parse_chosen_creature_type_static_scope_body`'s addition-suffix logic, extended to optionally accept `\"creature \"` before `\"types\"` \u2014 reused by both the existing single-subject dispatcher and the new compound one (no duplicated grammar).\n2. A new `parse_compound_you_control_chosen_type_static` in `type_change.rs` that delegates subject resolution **whole** to the already-generic `parse_continuous_subject_filter` (which already produces an `Or` filter for \"`X you control and Y you control`\" via `parse_controlled_compound_continuous_subject_filter`) \u2014 reused, not reimplemented \u2014 and only owns the predicate (chosen-type link + additive-suffix gate). Declines unless the resolved subject is a genuine `Or` of 2+ filters, so single-subject lines are left untouched for the existing sibling. Declines non-additive (CR 205.1a replacement) predicates, matching the same \"no over-claiming\" discipline #5219 added for its own compound-subject gate.\n3. Dispatch registration in `oracle_static/dispatch.rs` alongside the existing `parse_arcane_adaptation_chosen_type_static` call.\n4. A same-is-true tail prefix matcher + one `push_same_is_true_static_tail(...)` call in `oracle.rs` (parallel to the existing calls for `parse_chosen_creature_type_static_prefix` / `parse_every_creature_type_static_prefix`) so Rukarumel's trailing \"The same is true for...\" sentence is preserved as a visible `Unimplemented` residual rather than silently swallowed or causing the whole line to strict-fail \u2014 matching Arcane Adaptation/Maskwood Nexus's existing behavior exactly.\n5. Tests: a positive parse test on Rukarumel's verbatim text (asserting the `Or` affected filter, the `AddChosenSubtype{CreatureType}` modification, and the tail surviving as `Unimplemented`), plus decline/gate tests (single-subject forms still route to the existing handler unchanged; a non-additive/replacement compound predicate is correctly declined).\n\nNo new `ContinuousModification` variant, `Layer`, or runtime is needed \u2014 `AddChosenSubtype { kind: CreatureType }` is already fully wired (Arcane Adaptation/Xenograft/Lifecraft Engine already exercise it end-to-end).\n\n## CR references (to verify against `docs/MagicCompRules.txt` at implementation time)\n- CR 607.2d \u2014 chosen-value ability linking\n- CR 205.1b \u2014 additive type/subtype retention (\"in addition to its/their other types\")\n- CR 205.3m \u2014 creature types\n- CR 611.3 \u2014 a continuous static effect applies to every object its text indicates (Or-distributed affected set)\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-09T02:52:39.000Z",
